  "summary": {
    "en": {
      "caveats": "The framework's performance and utility were evaluated using a single disease (COVID-19) within a single state (Virginia).",
      "what": "The EpiFlow framework processes wastewater viral loads (WVL) and incorporates them into a time-varying forecasting model to predict COVID-19 hospital admissions. Tested across Virginia and its health regions, the framework uses entropy measures to assess predictability and causality tests to capture temporal dynamics, resulting in a 20 percentage point improvement in forecast coverage compared to baseline models.",
      "why": "It establishes that wastewater data can reliably improve real-time hospital burden forecasting even during challenging periods of low disease prevalence or delayed reporting, providing a validated method to maintain early-warning capabilities when clinical reporting declines."
